sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant UC as Use case
    participant DB as Service DB
    participant RL as Outbox relay (every replica, every 100 ms, SKIP LOCKED)
    participant K as Kafka
    UC->>DB: BEGIN#59; UPDATE aggregate#59; INSERT outbox row#59; COMMIT
    loop poll
        RL->>DB: BEGIN#59; SELECT … WHERE published_at IS NULL ORDER BY created_at LIMIT 500 FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
        DB-->>RL: batch
        RL->>K: send all (key = aggregate_id, acks=all, idempotent producer)
        K-->>RL: acks
        RL->>DB: UPDATE outbox SET published_at = now() WHERE id IN (…)#59; COMMIT
    end
    Note over RL,K: A crash after send and before commit re-sends the batch: consumers dedupe by eventId
